01:28:44.700 --> 01:28:46.700
We don't do that at ITPM.

01:28:46.700 --> 01:28:49.700
We're going to give you the tools, but we
need you to respond.

01:28:49.700 --> 01:28:50.700
Okay?

01:28:50.700 --> 01:28:53.700
You need to respond with work ethic.

01:28:53.700 --> 01:28:59.700
And work ethic is conscientiousness, not
passion, not motivation.

01:28:59.700 --> 01:29:00.700
Okay?

01:29:00.700 --> 01:29:03.700
Try to eliminate those words from your
vocabulary.

01:29:03.700 --> 01:29:08.700
Replace passion and motivation with
conscientiousness.

01:29:08.700 --> 01:29:10.700
It's way more important.

01:29:10.700 --> 01:29:12.700
But guys, don't be scared of the work.

01:29:12.700 --> 01:29:15.700
We're going to take you through all of
these processes.

01:29:15.700 --> 01:29:18.700
It's not as hard as you think.

01:29:18.700 --> 01:29:21.700
It just requires application and
conscientiousness.

01:29:21.700 --> 01:29:24.700
Once you understand it, it's
straightforward.

01:29:24.700 --> 01:29:30.700
And over time, your processes will get
quicker the more you practice.

01:29:30.700 --> 01:29:34.700
The hard yards in this game are put in
now.

01:29:34.700 --> 01:29:39.700
But it does get easier over time.

01:29:39.700 --> 01:29:42.700
So just stick at it.

01:29:42.700 --> 01:29:50.700
Next up in ITPM principles, free
information.

01:29:50.700 --> 01:29:56.700
When you're starting out learning how to
trade, it's important to get your hands
dirty.

01:29:56.700 --> 01:30:07.700
Getting your hands dirty in the data to
really understand the nuts and bolts of
financial markets and how to interpret the
data properly.

01:30:07.700 --> 01:30:18.700
At this stage, you absolutely do not need
to pay for third-party software and incur
expenses in an attempt to create
shortcuts.

01:30:18.700 --> 01:30:30.700
Your interpretation of publicly available
data is way more important than having a
software subscription.

01:30:30.700 --> 01:30:31.700
Think about it.

01:30:31.700 --> 01:30:37.700
What is the point of paying for software
and data if you don't even know where it
comes from?

01:30:37.700 --> 01:30:41.700
You don't even know how to understand and
interpret it.

01:30:41.700 --> 01:30:45.700
And you haven't even turned a profit in
your trading account yet.

01:30:45.700 --> 01:30:49.700
A software is not going to turn you into a
profitable trader.

01:30:49.700 --> 01:30:51.700
Only you can do that.

01:30:51.700 --> 01:31:00.700
You need to get, in the beginning, your
hands dirty in the data to truly
understand the nuts and bolts of this
business.

01:31:00.700 --> 01:31:05.700
To understand the underpinnings of the
financial markets.

01:31:05.700 --> 01:31:08.700
And you need to understand how to
interpret it properly.

01:31:08.700 --> 01:31:12.700
No software can replicate those two
endeavors.

01:31:12.700 --> 01:31:13.700
Okay?

01:31:13.700 --> 01:31:16.700
It's very important at the beginning of
your career to do that.

01:31:16.700 --> 01:31:27.700
You know, when we had graduates coming
from university onto the Goldman Sachs
trading desk, we knew that they had all
the resources at their fingertips.

01:31:27.700 --> 01:31:37.700
We knew we'd be giving them amazing
software, Bloomberg software, et cetera,
and they would have access to amazing data
sets.

01:31:37.700 --> 01:31:38.700
Okay?

01:31:38.700 --> 01:31:45.700
But we also knew that they didn't even
know where the data came from, what it
means, and how to interpret it.

01:31:45.700 --> 01:31:50.700
So we made them get their hands dirty for
at least the first three months.

01:31:50.700 --> 01:31:51.700
Okay?

01:31:51.700 --> 01:31:59.700
In building spreadsheets, crunching data,
and understanding all the processes, and
understanding the nuts and bolts of
financial markets.

01:31:59.700 --> 01:32:04.700
It's absolutely crucial in the beginning
stages of your development that you learn
how to do that.

01:32:04.700 --> 01:32:18.700
We stick to the principle of free
information, we look at publicly available
data sets, and we learn how to process
that data, and get an understanding of the
nuts and bolts of financial markets.

01:32:18.700 --> 01:32:27.700
One of the biggest secrets of the
financial education industry is that it's
totally possible to make money first with
free information.

01:32:27.700 --> 01:32:37.700
From the data, by getting your hands dirty
in the data, and understanding the
financial markets first.

01:32:37.700 --> 01:32:38.700
Why?

01:32:38.700 --> 01:32:43.700
Because they all want you to sign up for
recurring revenue products like software.

01:32:43.700 --> 01:32:44.700
Okay?

01:32:44.700 --> 01:32:59.700
A lot of this stuff gets sold to you as a
shortcut and a hack, and gets sold to you
as a panacea or a solution, okay, to your
problem of not being able to make money.

01:32:59.700 --> 01:33:02.700
The software will never give you the
answer, guys.

01:33:02.700 --> 01:33:03.700
Okay?

01:33:03.700 --> 01:33:13.700
The software will just give you data that
you can get elsewhere, but you can learn
how to get your hands dirty in the data,
and learn how to interpret it properly.

01:33:13.700 --> 01:33:14.700
Okay?

01:33:14.700 --> 01:33:20.700
You just have to be taught how to do it by
people who know how.

01:33:20.700 --> 01:33:22.700
So, professional traders.

01:33:22.700 --> 01:33:23.700
Okay?

01:33:23.700 --> 01:33:37.700
Then, and only then, are you allowed to
start subscribing to products that give
you a quick answer, or subscribe to
products that save you some time.

01:33:37.700 --> 01:33:38.700
Okay?

01:33:38.700 --> 01:33:47.700
Then, and only then, are you allowed to go
and spend money on third-party software
and pay for data.

01:33:47.700 --> 01:33:52.700
And even then, only if it makes sense to
do so.

01:33:52.700 --> 01:34:00.700
So, at the Institute, in the beginning, we
stick to this principle of making money
first.

01:34:00.700 --> 01:34:10.700
You open your trading account, you put
money into your account, and you make
money first, implementing what you have
learned in theory.

01:34:10.700 --> 01:34:19.700
And when you make money from it, maybe a
small percentage can be spent on softwares
later.

01:34:19.700 --> 01:34:20.700
Not now.

01:34:20.700 --> 01:34:21.700
Later.

01:34:21.700 --> 01:34:22.700
Okay?

01:34:22.700 --> 01:34:28.700
So, you start out with no resources prior
to ever paying for anything.

01:34:28.700 --> 01:34:33.700
It's a very important principle, because
it has a lot of ramifications.

01:34:33.700 --> 01:34:46.700
It means it forces you to get your hands
dirty, forces you to learn financial
markets properly, and it forces you to
understand how to interpret the publicly
available free information.

01:34:46.700 --> 01:34:47.700
Okay?

01:34:47.700 --> 01:34:52.700
That gives you a fantastic fundamental
crutch for the rest of your career.

01:34:52.700 --> 01:34:56.700
So, you may not even ever need to pay for
software.

01:34:56.700 --> 01:34:57.700
That's the beauty of it.

01:34:57.700 --> 01:35:07.700
So, we stick to this principle, because
it's very important to start off your
career getting your hands dirty from the
free information.

01:35:07.700 --> 01:35:21.700
Stick to the principle of making money
first from free information, never paying
for anything, and then if it makes sense
to do so in the future, then perhaps think
about it, if it adds value to your
trading.

01:35:21.700 --> 01:35:26.700
Next up, working smart, not hard.

01:35:26.700 --> 01:35:49.700
Once you've actually done the hard yards
of learning the theory, and then you move
on to implementation, of course, this
whole endeavor of trading in the same way
that a professional trader does, but in
the retail trading infrastructure as a
retail trader, it has to fit into your
regular weekly life.

01:35:49.700 --> 01:35:54.700
Now, earlier, we referred to work ethic,
okay?

01:35:54.700 --> 01:36:00.700
And when we did so, we referred to
conscientiousness, not passion or
motivation.

01:36:00.700 --> 01:36:06.700
And certainly here, not the amount of
hours you're willing to work per week.

01:36:06.700 --> 01:36:11.700
You can work for 50 hours a week on
trading and not make money.

01:36:11.700 --> 01:36:14.700
You need to work smart, okay?

